# CosmWasm Integration & Smart Contract Emissions - Custom Module Implementation

## Overview
Create a **custom ignite-scaffolded contracts module** that integrates CosmWasm smart contracting with the existing `x/emissions` module. This approach provides clean CLI integration, full control over business logic, and seamless emissions registry integration while maintaining the permissionless platform for contract funding.

## ⚠️ CRITICAL IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS
- **BUILD ON existing registry** - leverage the Open Module Registration infrastructure
- **PRESERVE all functionality** - existing emissions and module registration must continue working
- **LEAN V1 approach** - focus on core contract support, add staking in future versions
- **NO breaking changes** - chain must continue running identically during implementation
- **SECURE execution** - contracts run in sandboxed Wasm VM
- **CLEAN ARCHITECTURE** - custom module with standard ignite patterns

## Implementation Strategy: Custom Contracts Module

### Why Custom Module Over Direct x/wasmd Integration?
- ✅ **Automatic CLI Registration** - All commands work out of the box
- ✅ **Clean Module Structure** - Standard ignite patterns and conventions
- ✅ **Custom Business Logic** - Easy integration with emissions registry
- ✅ **Full Control** - Customize permissions, validation, and workflows
- ✅ **Maintainable Code** - Follows existing codebase patterns
- ✅ **Direct Integration** - Tight coupling with emissions module

